### Section-by-Section Summary

**Status vs Plan (Table)**
This table provides a high-level status update (as of 2026-10-25) for the IntarsiaML architecture. It categorizes components as **implemented**, **partial**, or **planned**.
*   **Implemented:** Rust host/server/CLI, CPU/CUDA/HIP backends, Metal backend, kernel registry, torch-free C ABI, quant formats (BF16, FP8, etc.), watchdog/supervisor, Prometheus metrics.
*   **Partial:** Backend trait, kernel registration, block library (GQA, GDN, etc.), recipes, plan compiler, scheduler, prefix cache, host-RAM KV tier, speculation, sampler, tool parsers, tensor parallelism, accuracy system, bench plugins, OpenAI/Anthropic APIs, containers/replay.
*   **Planned:** Vulkan/SYCL backend, autotuner/tuning DB, GGUF/AWQ/GPTQ quant formats, `intarsia-quant` crate, paged KV blocks.

